// ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
// ✦ Xiuu · Clawdy · Hooks and live data
// © 2026 Xiuu · Released under the MIT License, see LICENSE.
// ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
import { atom, read, update } from 'claude-code'
import type { EngineInterface, Register } from 'claude-code'

import type { Gauge, Git, Snapshot } from '../types'
import { ANIMATE, CLAWD_SHOW, FRAME_MS, GIT_MIN_GAP, PET, REFRESH_EVERY, TOOL_MOODS, USAGE } from './config'
import { isAnimated } from './effort'
import { drawDesktop } from './hud-desktop'
import { drawHud } from './hud'
import { cellsOf, frameFor, HOP_ARC } from './pet'
import type { Mood } from './pet'

const snapshot = atom({ plugin: 'clawdy', key: 'snapshot' } as const, null)
const effortSeen = atom({ plugin: 'clawdy', key: 'effort' } as const, null)
const frame = atom({ plugin: 'clawdy', key: 'frame' } as const, 0)
// the desktop has no Raster to repaint: its band redraws on this, read by the desktop path alone
const deskTick = atom({ plugin: 'clawdy', key: 'deskTick' } as const, 0)

// ============ DATA ============

let lastGitAt = 0
let lastGit: Git | null = null

async function readGit($: EngineInterface, cwd: string, now: number): Promise<Git | null> {
  if (now - lastGitAt < GIT_MIN_GAP) return lastGit
  lastGitAt = now
  try {
    const status = await $.process.run(
      ['git', '-C', cwd, '--no-optional-locks', 'status', '--porcelain=v2', '--branch'],
      { timeoutMs: 3_000 },
    )
    if (status.exitCode !== 0) return (lastGit = null)

    let branch = ''
    let ahead = 0
    let behind = 0
    let changed = 0
    for (const line of status.stdout.split('\n')) {
      if (line.startsWith('# branch.head ')) branch = line.slice(14).trim()
      else if (line.startsWith('# branch.ab ')) {
        const [a = '0', b = '0'] = line.slice(12).trim().split(' ')
        ahead = Math.abs(parseInt(a, 10)) || 0
        behind = Math.abs(parseInt(b, 10)) || 0
      } else if (line && !line.startsWith('#')) changed += 1
    }

    let added = 0
    let deleted = 0
    const diff = await $.process.run(['git', '-C', cwd, '--no-optional-locks', 'diff', 'HEAD', '--shortstat'], {
      timeoutMs: 3_000,
    })
    if (diff.exitCode === 0) {
      added = parseInt(diff.stdout.match(/(\d+) insertion/)?.[1] ?? '0', 10)
      deleted = parseInt(diff.stdout.match(/(\d+) deletion/)?.[1] ?? '0', 10)
    }

    return (lastGit = { branch: branch === '(detached)' ? 'detached' : branch, added, deleted, changed, ahead, behind })
  } catch {
    return lastGit
  }
}

let lastSettingsEffort: string | undefined

// ---- account usage, polled ----

type Polled = { session?: Gauge; week?: Gauge; at: number }
let polled: Polled | null = null

async function pollUsage($: EngineInterface): Promise<void> {
  try {
    const auth = await $.session.authorize()
    if (auth?.kind !== 'bearer') return
    const res = await $.http.fetch(USAGE.url, {
      auth: auth.handle,
      headers: { 'anthropic-beta': USAGE.beta, accept: 'application/json' },
    })
    if (!res.ok) return
    const data = JSON.parse(res.text) as Record<string, { utilization?: number | null; resets_at?: string | null } | null>
    const gauge = (kind: string): Gauge | undefined => {
      const w = data[kind]
      return typeof w?.utilization === 'number' ? { percent: w.utilization, resetsAt: w.resets_at ?? undefined } : undefined
    }
    polled = { session: gauge('five_hour'), week: gauge('seven_day'), at: await $.clock.now() }
    await refresh($)
  } catch {
    // the session's own readings stand
  }
}

async function settingsEffort($: EngineInterface, model: string): Promise<string | undefined> {
  const settings = (await $.settings.read({})) as unknown as {
    effortLevel?: string
    modelSettings?: Record<string, { effortLevel?: string }>
  }
  return settings.modelSettings?.[model.replace(/\[.*\]$/, '')]?.effortLevel ?? settings.effortLevel
}

async function refresh($: EngineInterface): Promise<void> {
  const [usage, model, cwd, now] = await Promise.all([
    $.session.usage(),
    $.session.model(),
    $.session.cwd(),
    $.clock.now(),
  ])
  const git = await readGit($, cwd, now)
  const fromSettings = await settingsEffort($, model)
  // a change in settings (/effort) is newer than the level the last request carried
  if (fromSettings !== lastSettingsEffort && lastSettingsEffort !== undefined && fromSettings) {
    await update($, effortSeen, () => fromSettings)
  }
  lastSettingsEffort = fromSettings
  const effort = (await read($, effortSeen)) ?? fromSettings
  const windowOf = (kind: string): Gauge | undefined => {
    const r = usage.rateLimits.find(l => l.kind === kind)
    return r ? { percent: r.percentUsed, resetsAt: r.resetsAt } : undefined
  }
  const account = polled && now - polled.at < USAGE.pollEvery * 2 ? polled : null

  const next: Snapshot = {
    model,
    effort,
    cwd,
    costUsd: usage.cost?.usd,
    home: (await $.env.get('USERPROFILE')) ?? (await $.env.get('HOME')),
    context: usage.context,
    session: account?.session ?? windowOf('five_hour'),
    week: account?.week ?? windowOf('seven_day'),
    git,
  }
  await update($, snapshot, () => next)
}

// ============ ANIMATION ============

// whether Claude is working, as the band last drew it; the shine and Clawd follow it
let isBusy = false

async function nextFrame($: EngineInterface): Promise<void> {
  if (ANIMATE === 'off' || (ANIMATE === 'working' && !isBusy)) return
  const snap = await read($, snapshot)
  if (!isAnimated(snap?.effort)) return
  await update($, frame, n => (n + 1) % 1_000_000)
}

// ============ PET ============

// the band's site, so a tick can repaint Clawd alone
let bandId: string | null = null
let lastActivity = 0
let pose: { mood: Mood; until: number } | null = null
let tick = 0
let shownCells = ''

type Act = { mood: Mood; ms: number; isNight?: boolean }

// the /clawd show: acts played back to back, ahead of everything else
let show: { acts: readonly Act[]; startedAt: number } | null = null

function showAct(now: number): Act | null {
  if (!show) return null
  let elapsed = now - show.startedAt
  for (const act of show.acts) {
    if (elapsed < act.ms) return act
    elapsed -= act.ms
  }
  show = null
  return null
}

function moodAt(now: number): Mood {
  if (pose && now < pose.until) return pose.mood
  if (isBusy) return 'think'
  if (lastActivity && now - lastActivity > PET.sleepAfter) return 'sleep'
  return 'idle'
}

function isNightAt(now: number): boolean {
  const hour = new Date(now).getHours()
  const { from, to } = PET.night
  return from <= to ? hour >= from && hour < to : hour >= from || hour < to
}

function petCells(now: number): string {
  const act = showAct(now)
  return cellsOf(
    frameFor(act?.mood ?? moodAt(now), tick, {
      isNight: act?.isNight ?? isNightAt(now),
    }),
  )
}

/** Holds a mood for `ms`, the way a tool, an error or the end of a turn calls for. */
async function strike($: EngineInterface, mood: Mood, ms: number): Promise<void> {
  const now = await $.clock.now()
  pose = { mood, until: now + ms }
  lastActivity = now
}

// when a desktop band last drew; 0 while none has, so a terminal session never pays for it
let deskSeenAt = 0
const DESK_GONE_MS = 2_000

/** Clawd's frame now, for the desktop band (the terminal packs its own with petCells). */
function petFrame(now: number): ReturnType<typeof frameFor> {
  const act = showAct(now)
  return frameFor(act?.mood ?? moodAt(now), tick, { isNight: act?.isNight ?? isNightAt(now) })
}

async function petTick($: EngineInterface): Promise<void> {
  tick = (tick + 1) % 1_000_000
  if (deskSeenAt !== 0 && (await $.clock.now()) - deskSeenAt < DESK_GONE_MS) await update($, deskTick, () => tick)
  if (!bandId) return
  const cells = petCells(await $.clock.now())
  if (cells === shownCells) return
  shownCells = cells
  await $.ui.blit({ requestId: bandId, key: 'pet', cells })
}

const pad2 = (n: number) => String(n).padStart(2, '0')

// ============ HOOKS ============
// Subagents raise the same events with an `agentId`: Clawd and the effort follow
// the main conversation alone.

export const register: Register = on => {
  on('session.start', async ($, e, next) => {
    const result = await next(e)
    await refresh($)
    $.clock.every(REFRESH_EVERY, () => refresh($))
    $.clock.every(FRAME_MS, () => nextFrame($))
    lastActivity = await $.clock.now()
    if (PET.show) {
      $.clock.every(PET.frameMs, () => petTick($))
      await $.command.register({
        name: 'clawd',
        description: `Clawd plays every animation, or one: ${CLAWD_SHOW.acts.map(a => a.name).join(', ')}; add night for his cap`,
      })
    }
    $.clock.after(0, () => pollUsage($))
    $.clock.every(USAGE.pollEvery, () => pollUsage($))
    return result
  })

  on('turn.step', async function* ($, e, next) {
    if (!e.agentId && typeof e.effort === 'string') await update($, effortSeen, () => e.effort as string)
    return yield* next(e)
  })

  on('prompt.submit', async ($, e, next) => {
    isBusy = true
    lastActivity = await $.clock.now()
    return next(e)
  })

  on('tool.call', async ($, e, next) => {
    if (e.agentId) return next(e)
    await strike($, TOOL_MOODS[e.tool] ?? 'think', PET.poseMs)
    const result = await next(e)
    if (result.isError) await strike($, 'sad', PET.sadMs)
    await refresh($)
    return result
  })

  on('session.compact', async ($, e, next) => {
    if (e.agentId || e.trigger === 'precompute') return next(e)
    pose = { mood: 'compact', until: Number.POSITIVE_INFINITY }
    try {
      return await next(e)
    } finally {
      pose = { mood: 'compact', until: (await $.clock.now()) + PET.settleMs }
    }
  })

  on('turn.complete', async ($, e, next) => {
    const result = await next(e)
    if (e.agentId) return result
    isBusy = false
    // a hop only for a real answer: an interrupt (Esc) leaves him be, an API error saddens him
    if (e.reason === 'answer') await strike($, 'party', PET.partyHops * HOP_ARC.length * PET.frameMs)
    if (e.reason === 'error') await strike($, 'sad', PET.sadMs)
    await refresh($)
    return result
  })

  on('command.run', { command: 'clawd' }, async ($, e) => {
    // an act to hold, `night` for the cap, or both; the show is a demo, so without `night`
    // Clawd plays it bareheaded at any hour, and with it, in his cap
    const words = e.args.trim().toLowerCase().split(/\s+/).filter(Boolean)
    const now = await $.clock.now()
    const clock = new Date(now)
    const time = `Clawd's clock: ${pad2(clock.getHours())}:${pad2(clock.getMinutes())}`
    const layers = { isNight: words.includes('night') }
    const rest = words.filter(w => w !== 'night')
    const suffix = layers.isNight ? ' (cap on)' : ''

    if (rest.length === 0) {
      show = { acts: CLAWD_SHOW.acts.map(a => ({ ...a, ...layers })), startedAt: now }
      const seconds = Math.round(CLAWD_SHOW.acts.reduce((sum, a) => sum + a.ms, 0) / 1000)
      return { text: `Clawd's show${suffix}: ${CLAWD_SHOW.acts.map(a => a.name).join(' → ')} (${seconds} s). ${time}` }
    }
    const act = CLAWD_SHOW.acts.find(a => a.name === rest[0])
    if (!act || rest.length > 1) {
      return { text: `Try an act: ${CLAWD_SHOW.acts.map(a => a.name).join(', ')}; add night for his cap.` }
    }
    show = { acts: [{ ...act, ...layers, ms: CLAWD_SHOW.hold }], startedAt: now }
    return { text: `Clawd: ${act.name}${suffix}, ${CLAWD_SHOW.hold / 1000} s. ${time}` }
  })

  on('ui.render', { component: 'AbovePrompt' }, async ($, e, next) => {
    const snap = await read($, snapshot)
    if (e.props.hasSurvey || !snap) return next(e)

    const now = await $.clock.now()
    bandId = e.requestId
    isBusy = e.props.isWorking
    if (isBusy) lastActivity = now
    const isMoving = ANIMATE === 'always' || (ANIMATE === 'working' && e.props.isWorking)

    // the desktop gets its own drawing; every other surface goes on below, as it always has
    if (e.surface === 'desktop') {
      const desk = $.ui.resolve(e)
      if ('Svg' in desk) {
        deskSeenAt = now
        await read($, deskTick)
        return drawDesktop(
          { Svg: desk.Svg },
          { snap, columns: e.props.bodyColumns, now, frame: await read($, frame), isMoving, pet: PET.show ? petFrame(now) : null },
        )
      }
    }

    const table = $.ui.resolve(e)
    const { Box, Text } = table
    const Raster = 'Raster' in table ? table.Raster : undefined
    shownCells = PET.show ? petCells(now) : ''
    return drawHud(
      { Box, Text, Raster },
      {
        snap,
        columns: e.props.bodyColumns,
        now,
        frame: await read($, frame),
        isMoving,
        pet: PET.show ? shownCells : null,
      },
    )
  })
}

