// ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
// ✦ Xiuu · Clawdy · Config
// © 2026 Xiuu · Released under the MIT License, see LICENSE.
// ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

// ============ PALETTE ============
// Apple system colors, dark appearance.
export const COLORS = {
  text: '#F5F5F7',
  muted: '#8E8E93',
  faint: '#636366',
  card: '#3A3A3C',
  track: '#2C2C2E',
  accent: '#0A84FF',
  warn: '#FF9F0A',
  alert: '#FF453A',
  add: '#30D158',
  remove: '#FF453A',
} as const

// ============ HEAT SCALE ============
// Every bar runs through it from its left edge: a low gauge shows only green,
// a full one reaches red. Stops are spread evenly across the bar.
export const HEAT = ['#30D158', '#A6E22E', '#FFD60A', '#FF9F0A', '#FF453A'] as const

// ============ THRESHOLDS ============
// A card's border takes the warn or alert color past these.
export const WARN_AT = 75
export const ALERT_AT = 90

// ============ CARDS ============
export const CARD_TITLES = {
  model: { icon: '🧠', title: 'Model' },
  context: { icon: '📊', title: 'Context' },
  usage: { icon: '⏳', title: 'Usage' },
  project: { icon: '📂', title: 'Project' },
} as const

// ============ EFFORT ============
// One look per level, after /effort: a solid color, a moving shine, or a rainbow.
export type EffortLook =
  | { kind: 'solid'; color: string }
  | { kind: 'shine'; color: string; shine: string; width: number }
  | { kind: 'rainbow'; saturation: number; lightness: number; spread: number; speed: number }

export const EFFORT: Record<string, { label: string; look: EffortLook }> = {
  low: { label: 'Low', look: { kind: 'solid', color: '#FFD60A' } },
  medium: { label: 'Medium', look: { kind: 'solid', color: '#30D158' } },
  high: { label: 'High', look: { kind: 'solid', color: '#64D2FF' } },
  xhigh: { label: 'X-High', look: { kind: 'shine', color: '#BF5AF2', shine: '#F4E3FF', width: 2 } },
  max: { label: 'Max', look: { kind: 'rainbow', saturation: 90, lightness: 66, spread: 55, speed: 14 } },
}

// ============ PET ============
// Clawd, left of the cards. Colors are 0xRRGGBB; times in ms.
export const PET = {
  show: true,
  body: 0xd77757, // Claude Code's own clawd_body, rgb(215,119,87)
  lid: 0x8f4a35,
  spark: 0xffd60a,
  alert: 0xff453a,
  muted: 0x8e8e93,
  frameMs: 110,
  blinkEvery: 44, // ticks between blinks, in every act; a blink lasts two
  steamTicks: 4, // ticks per step of the coffee's steam
  poseMs: 1_500,
  partyHops: 4, // hops when an answer lands, about 2.6 s, then his coffee
  sadMs: 1_800,
  settleMs: 800, // how long he stays flat once a compaction is done
  sleepAfter: 180_000,
  // the night cap, from `from` to `to` o'clock, local time
  night: { from: 0, to: 6 },
  // what he works with: the pan and pancake, the sheet, the magnifier, the cap, the mug, his tears
  props: {
    pan: 0x8e8e93,
    panHandle: 0x6e6e73, // steel, a shade darker than the pan
    pancake: 0xf2c14e,
    steam: 0xd1d1d6,
    paper: 0xf5f5f7,
    ink: 0x48484a,
    rim: 0x5e7a99,
    collar: 0x2c3e55,
    lensHandle: 0xf2b033,
    glass: 0x8fd3f5,
    glint: 0xe3f6ff,
    cap: 0x5e5ce6,
    capBand: 0xf5f5f7,
    mug: 0xf5f5f7,
    coffee: 0x6e4b3a,
    tear: 0x64d2ff,
  },
} as const

// What Clawd does while a tool runs: writes on edits, takes the magnifier to read or
// search, code and web alike. Any other tool, commands included, and thinking: he cooks.
export const TOOL_MOODS: Record<string, 'type' | 'search'> = {
  Edit: 'type',
  Write: 'type',
  NotebookEdit: 'type',
  Read: 'search',
  Grep: 'search',
  Glob: 'search',
  WebFetch: 'search',
  WebSearch: 'search',
}

// /clawd plays the show, in the order a turn goes; /clawd <name> holds one act for `hold` ms;
// /clawd night plays the whole show with the night cap on.
export const CLAWD_SHOW: {
  hold: number
  acts: readonly { name: string; mood: 'idle' | 'think' | 'type' | 'search' | 'sad' | 'party' | 'sleep' | 'compact'; ms: number }[]
} = {
  hold: 10_000,
  acts: [
    { name: 'idle', mood: 'idle', ms: 3_000 },
    { name: 'cook', mood: 'think', ms: 5_000 },
    { name: 'search', mood: 'search', ms: 4_000 },
    { name: 'write', mood: 'type', ms: 5_000 },
    { name: 'party', mood: 'party', ms: 2_500 },
    { name: 'sad', mood: 'sad', ms: 3_000 },
    { name: 'compact', mood: 'compact', ms: 3_000 },
    { name: 'sleep', mood: 'sleep', ms: 4_000 },
  ],
}

// ============ ANIMATION ============
// 'working': the shine moves while Claude works, still otherwise. 'always' or 'off'.
export const ANIMATE: 'working' | 'always' | 'off' = 'working'
export const FRAME_MS = 90

// ============ CONTENT ============
// Cost is the API price of the session, not what a subscription pays.
export const SHOW_COST = false

// ============ TIMING (ms) ============
export const REFRESH_EVERY = 15_000
export const GIT_MIN_GAP = 4_000

// ============ USAGE POLL ============
// The account's 5h and 7d windows, every session and device included, read
// with the session's own credential (the plugin never sees it). Between polls,
// and when the poll fails, the readings of this session's last response stand.
export const USAGE = {
  url: 'https://api.anthropic.com/api/oauth/usage',
  beta: 'oauth-2025-04-20',
  pollEvery: 60_000,
} as const

// ============ LAYOUT ============
// Columns the band needs for each arrangement of the cards.
export const ROW_FROM = 112
export const GRID_FROM = 64
export const CARD_GAP = 1
export const CARD_BORDER = 'round'

// ============ DESKTOP ============
// The Desktop app draws the band as one SVG, scaled to fit its slot. Sizes are the SVG's own pixels.
export const DESKTOP = {
  pxPerColumn: 8, // design width: the band's columns times this
  pixel: { w: 4, h: 8 }, // one of Clawd's pixels, as tall for its width as the terminal draws it
  font: "'Segoe UI', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, system-ui, sans-serif",
  fontSize: 13,
  pad: 4,
  gap: 8,
  // a card as tight as the terminal's: a title and two lines (their baselines below its top)
  card: { height: 64, radius: 8, inset: 10, rowFrom: 190, lines: { title: 19, mid: 38, low: 56 } }, // four in a row from rowFrom px a card
  bar: { block: 4, gap: 1, height: 5, lift: 8 }, // lift: how far above its text line a bar's top sits
  // follows the system's light or dark appearance
  dark: { text: '#F5F5F7', muted: '#8E8E93', faint: '#636366', fill: 'rgba(255,255,255,0.03)', stroke: 'rgba(255,255,255,0.13)', track: 'rgba(255,255,255,0.10)' },
  light: { text: '#1D1D1F', muted: '#6E6E73', faint: '#AEAEB2', fill: 'rgba(0,0,0,0.02)', stroke: 'rgba(0,0,0,0.13)', track: 'rgba(0,0,0,0.08)' },
} as const

// ============ GLYPHS ============
export const GLYPHS = {
  fill: '━',
  track: '━',
  dot: '·',
  branch: '⎇',
  ahead: '↑',
  behind: '↓',
  reset: '↻',
  clean: '✓',
} as const

