// ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
// ✦ Xiuu · Clawdy · Effort looks
// © 2026 Xiuu · Released under the MIT License, see LICENSE.
// ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
import { COLORS, EFFORT } from './config'
import { capitalize, hsl, mix } from './format'

export type Glyph = { char: string; color: string }

/** Whether this effort level has a look that moves. */
export function isAnimated(effort: string | undefined): boolean {
  const kind = effort ? EFFORT[effort]?.look.kind : undefined
  return kind === 'shine' || kind === 'rainbow'
}

/** The effort's label, one color per character, at animation `frame`. */
export function effortGlyphs(effort: string, frame: number, isMoving: boolean): Glyph[] {
  const entry = EFFORT[effort]
  const chars = [...(entry?.label ?? capitalize(effort))]
  // a level this file does not know yet still shows, in the accent color
  if (!entry) return chars.map(char => ({ char, color: COLORS.accent }))

  const look = entry.look
  switch (look.kind) {
    case 'solid':
      return chars.map(char => ({ char, color: look.color }))

    case 'shine': {
      // a bright band sweeps left to right, then waits off the edge before the next pass
      const cycle = chars.length + look.width * 4
      const center = isMoving ? (frame % cycle) - look.width : -99
      return chars.map((char, i) => {
        const glow = Math.max(0, 1 - Math.abs(i - center) / look.width)
        return { char, color: mix(look.color, look.shine, glow) }
      })
    }

    case 'rainbow': {
      const shift = isMoving ? frame * look.speed : 0
      return chars.map((char, i) => ({ char, color: hsl((i * look.spread + shift) % 360, look.saturation, look.lightness) }))
    }
  }
}

