// ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
// ✦ Xiuu · Clawdy · Cards
// © 2026 Xiuu · Released under the MIT License, see LICENSE.
// ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
import type { Elements, RenderElement } from 'claude-code'

import type { Gauge, Snapshot } from '../types'
import { CARD_BORDER, CARD_GAP, CARD_TITLES, COLORS, GLYPHS, GRID_FROM, HEAT, PET, ROW_FROM, SHOW_COST, WARN_AT } from './config'
import { effortGlyphs } from './effort'
import { formatModel, formatReset, formatTokens, scale, shortPath, tone } from './format'
import { PET_COLS, PET_ROWS } from './pet'

type Ui = Pick<Elements['terminal'], 'Box' | 'Text'> & { Raster?: Elements['terminal']['Raster'] }

export type HudInput = {
  snap: Snapshot
  columns: number
  now: number
  frame: number
  isMoving: boolean
  /** Clawd's current cells, or null when he is not drawn. */
  pet: string | null
}

const clamp = (n: number) => Math.max(0, Math.min(100, Math.round(n)))

// ============ PIECES ============

/** A thin bar whose filled part runs through the heat scale, green to red. */
function bar({ Text }: Ui, percent: number | undefined, width: number) {
  const filled = Math.round((clamp(percent ?? 0) * width) / 100)
  const cells: RenderElement[] = []
  for (let i = 0; i < filled; i++) {
    cells.push(<Text color={scale(HEAT, width > 1 ? i / (width - 1) : 0)}>{GLYPHS.fill}</Text>)
  }
  return (
    <Text>
      {cells}
      <Text color={COLORS.track}>{GLYPHS.track.repeat(Math.max(0, width - filled))}</Text>
    </Text>
  )
}

/** A percent in the color of the point its bar stops at. */
function percentText({ Text }: Ui, percent: number | undefined) {
  if (percent === undefined) return <Text color={COLORS.faint}>-</Text>
  const p = clamp(percent)
  return (
    <Text bold color={scale(HEAT, p / 100)}>
      {`${p}%`}
    </Text>
  )
}

function row(ui: Ui, width: number, left: RenderElement, right?: RenderElement) {
  const { Box } = ui
  return (
    <Box flexDirection="row" justifyContent="space-between" width={width}>
      {left}
      {right ?? null}
    </Box>
  )
}

/** The card's name: icon and bold title, the one bold line of every card. */
function title({ Text }: Ui, which: keyof typeof CARD_TITLES) {
  const t = CARD_TITLES[which]
  return <Text bold color={COLORS.text}>{`${t.icon} ${t.title}`}</Text>
}

function card(ui: Ui, key: string, width: number, rows: RenderElement[], accent?: string) {
  const { Box } = ui
  return (
    <Box
      key={key}
      flexDirection="column"
      width={width}
      flexShrink={0}
      paddingX={1}
      borderStyle={CARD_BORDER}
      borderColor={accent ?? COLORS.card}
    >
      {rows}
    </Box>
  )
}

// ============ CARDS ============

function modelCard(ui: Ui, { snap, frame, isMoving }: HudInput, width: number, inner: number) {
  const { Text } = ui
  const effort = snap.effort ? effortGlyphs(snap.effort, frame, isMoving).map(g => <Text color={g.color}>{g.char}</Text>) : []
  return card(ui, 'model', width, [
    row(ui, inner, title(ui, 'model')),
    row(
      ui,
      inner,
      <Text color={COLORS.text} wrap="truncate-end">
        {formatModel(snap.model)}
      </Text>,
      SHOW_COST && snap.costUsd !== undefined ? <Text color={COLORS.muted}>{`$${snap.costUsd.toFixed(2)}`}</Text> : undefined,
    ),
    <Text>{effort}</Text>,
  ])
}

function contextCard(ui: Ui, { snap }: HudInput, width: number, inner: number) {
  const { Text } = ui
  const ctx = snap.context
  // before the session's first answer there is no reading yet: an empty window reads 0
  const p = ctx.percent ?? 0
  return card(
    ui,
    'context',
    width,
    [
      row(ui, inner, title(ui, 'context'), percentText(ui, p)),
      bar(ui, p, inner),
      <Text color={COLORS.muted} wrap="truncate-end">
        {`${formatTokens(ctx.tokens ?? 0)} / ${formatTokens(ctx.window)}`}
      </Text>,
    ],
    p >= WARN_AT ? tone(p) : undefined,
  )
}

function usageCard(ui: Ui, { snap, now }: HudInput, width: number, inner: number) {
  const { Box, Text } = ui
  const nameWidth = 3
  const pctWidth = 5
  const resetWidth = 10
  const barWidth = Math.max(4, inner - nameWidth - pctWidth - resetWidth)

  // one window per line: its name, its bar, its percent, and when it resets
  const line = (key: string, name: string, gauge: Gauge | undefined) => {
    const reset = formatReset(gauge?.resetsAt, now)
    return (
      <Box key={key} flexDirection="row" width={inner}>
        <Text color={COLORS.muted}>{name.padEnd(nameWidth)}</Text>
        {bar(ui, gauge?.percent, barWidth)}
        <Box width={pctWidth} justifyContent="flex-end">
          {percentText(ui, gauge?.percent)}
        </Box>
        <Box width={resetWidth} justifyContent="flex-end">
          <Text color={COLORS.muted}>{reset ? `${GLYPHS.reset} ${reset}` : ''}</Text>
        </Box>
      </Box>
    )
  }

  const worst = Math.max(snap.session?.percent ?? 0, snap.week?.percent ?? 0)
  return card(
    ui,
    'usage',
    width,
    [row(ui, inner, title(ui, 'usage')), line('5h', '5h', snap.session), line('7d', '7d', snap.week)],
    worst >= WARN_AT ? tone(worst) : undefined,
  )
}

function projectCard(ui: Ui, { snap }: HudInput, width: number, inner: number) {
  const { Text } = ui
  const g = snap.git
  const sync = g
    ? [g.ahead ? `${GLYPHS.ahead}${g.ahead}` : '', g.behind ? `${GLYPHS.behind}${g.behind}` : ''].filter(Boolean).join(' ')
    : ''
  const isClean = g !== null && !g.added && !g.deleted && !g.changed

  // one layout wherever he works: the folder, always; its git state below, when it has one
  return card(ui, 'project', width, [
    row(ui, inner, title(ui, 'project'), sync ? <Text color={COLORS.muted}>{sync}</Text> : undefined),
    <Text color={COLORS.text} wrap="truncate-start">
      {shortPath(snap.cwd, snap.home)}
    </Text>,
    g ? (
      <Text wrap="truncate-end">
        <Text color={COLORS.muted}>{`${GLYPHS.branch} ${g.branch}`}</Text>
        {isClean ? <Text color={COLORS.add}>{`   ${GLYPHS.clean} clean`}</Text> : null}
        {g.added ? <Text color={COLORS.add}>{`   +${g.added}`}</Text> : null}
        {g.deleted ? <Text color={COLORS.remove}>{`  -${g.deleted}`}</Text> : null}
      </Text>
    ) : (
      <Text color={COLORS.faint}>no git</Text>
    ),
  ])
}

// ============ LAYOUT ============

export function drawHud(ui: Ui, input: HudInput): RenderElement {
  const { Box, Raster } = ui
  const petWidth = PET_COLS + CARD_GAP
  const hasPet = PET.show && Raster !== undefined && input.pet !== null && input.columns - petWidth >= GRID_FROM
  const cols = hasPet ? input.columns - petWidth : input.columns
  const perRow = cols >= ROW_FROM ? 4 : cols >= GRID_FROM ? 2 : 1
  const width = Math.floor((cols - CARD_GAP * (perRow - 1)) / perRow)
  const inner = Math.max(8, width - 4)

  const cards = [
    modelCard(ui, input, width, inner),
    contextCard(ui, input, width, inner),
    usageCard(ui, input, width, inner),
    projectCard(ui, input, width, inner),
  ]

  const rows: RenderElement[] = []
  for (let i = 0; i < cards.length; i += perRow) {
    rows.push(
      <Box key={`row${i}`} flexDirection="row" gap={CARD_GAP}>
        {cards.slice(i, i + perRow)}
      </Box>,
    )
  }
  const grid = <Box flexDirection="column">{rows}</Box>
  if (!hasPet || !Raster || input.pet === null) return grid

  return (
    <Box flexDirection="row" gap={CARD_GAP} alignItems="center">
      <Raster key="pet" columns={PET_COLS} rows={PET_ROWS} cells={input.pet} />
      {grid}
    </Box>
  )
}

