// ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
// ✦ Xiuu · Clawdy · Clawd, the pet
// © 2026 Xiuu · Released under the MIT License, see LICENSE.
// ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
import { PET } from './config'

// Clawd is drawn the way Claude Code draws him: quadrant blocks, two pixels
// across and two down per cell, the terminal's background showing through his
// eyes. A frame is a list of colored pixels (later ones on top) plus a few
// glyphs; `cellsOf` packs it for a Raster, two colors per cell at most.

export type Mood = 'idle' | 'think' | 'type' | 'search' | 'sad' | 'party' | 'sleep' | 'compact'

/** What holds through every act: the night cap. */
export type Extras = { isNight: boolean }

type Px = [x: number, y: number, color: number]
type Glyph = { cx: number; cy: number; char: string; color: number }
type Frame = { px: Px[]; glyphs: Glyph[] }

export const PET_COLS = 14
export const PET_ROWS = 5
const W = PET_COLS * 2
const H = PET_ROWS * 2
const SPRITE_W = 18
const BASE_Y = 4 // Clawd's top row, so his three cell rows are the grid's last three
// Clawd only moves in steps of two pixels: on an even offset every cell holds the
// same quadrants as Claude Code's own drawing, and he keeps his exact silhouette.
const CENTER_X = Math.floor((W - SPRITE_W) / 4) * 2
const AT_WORK_X = 0 // left, leaving the right side to what he works on
/** One hop of the party, a height per tick; its length sets how long a hop lasts. */
export const HOP_ARC = [0, 2, 2, 2, 0, 0]

// ============ CLAWD ============

type Pose = {
  eyes?: 'center' | 'right' | 'closed'
  arms?: 'out' | 'up' | 'down' | 'hold' | 'holdUp' | 'reach' | 'reachUp'
  shape?: 'full' | 'squished' | 'flat'
  cap?: boolean
  /** Shut for a blink: the lids close where the eyes look, so they never jump. */
  isBlinking?: boolean
}

function rect(x0: number, y0: number, x1: number, y1: number, color: number): Px[] {
  const px: Px[] = []
  for (let y = y0; y <= y1; y++) for (let x = x0; x <= x1; x++) px.push([x, y, color])
  return px
}

/** Clawd's pixels at offset (ox, oy), in a pose. */
function clawd(ox: number, oy: number, pose: Pose): Px[] {
  const px: Px[] = []
  const put = (x: number, y: number, color: number = PET.body) => px.push([ox + x, oy + y, color])
  const span = (y: number, from: number, to: number, skip: number[] = []) => {
    for (let x = from; x <= to; x++) if (!skip.includes(x)) put(x, y)
  }

  const eyes = pose.eyes ?? 'center'
  const holes = eyes === 'right' ? [6, 13] : [5, 12]
  const isShut = eyes === 'closed' || pose.isBlinking === true
  const shape = pose.shape ?? 'full'

  // the body, full height or pressed down; the eyes sit on its top row
  const eyeRow = shape === 'full' ? 1 : 2
  if (shape === 'full') (span(0, 3, 14), span(1, 3, 14, holes), span(2, 3, 14), span(3, 3, 14))
  if (shape === 'squished') (span(1, 2, 15), span(2, 2, 15, holes), span(3, 2, 15))
  if (shape === 'flat') (span(2, 1, 16, holes), span(3, 1, 16))
  // shut eyes are lids, a darker orange, so his face stays a face
  if (isShut) for (const x of holes) put(x, eyeRow, PET.lid)

  // arms: out by default, raised, dropped, or the right one holding what he works on
  const arms = shape === 'full' ? (pose.arms ?? 'out') : 'out'
  if (shape !== 'full') (span(3, 0, 1), span(3, 16, 17))
  else if (arms === 'up') (put(2, 1), put(1, 0), put(15, 1), put(16, 0))
  else if (arms === 'down') (span(3, 1, 2), span(3, 15, 16))
  else {
    span(2, 1, 2)
    if (arms === 'hold') put(15, 2)
    else if (arms === 'holdUp') put(15, 1)
    else if (arms === 'reach') span(2, 15, 17)
    else if (arms === 'reachUp') (put(15, 2), span(1, 16, 17))
    else span(2, 15, 16)
  }

  for (const x of [4, 6, 11, 13]) put(x, 4)

  // the night cap: a white band on his head, the cap drooping left, away from
  // what he works on at his right, a pompom at its tip
  if (pose.cap) {
    const c = PET.props
    const top = shape === 'full' ? 0 : shape === 'squished' ? 1 : 2
    px.push(...rect(ox + 4, oy + top - 1, ox + 13, oy + top - 1, c.capBand))
    px.push(...rect(ox + 4, oy + top - 2, ox + 12, oy + top - 2, c.cap))
    px.push(...rect(ox + 3, oy + top - 3, ox + 8, oy + top - 3, c.cap))
    put(2, top - 2, c.cap)
    put(1, top - 1, c.capBand)
  }
  return px
}

// ============ WHAT HE WORKS ON ============

type Draw = (ox: number, oy: number, pose: Pose) => Px[]

/** Pancakes: sizzle, toss, a flip in the air, land. One cycle is 16 ticks. */
function cooking(draw: Draw, t: number): Px[] {
  const c = PET.props
  const beat = t % 16
  const isToss = beat === 6
  const top = isToss ? 5 : 6
  const px = draw(AT_WORK_X, BASE_Y, { eyes: 'right', arms: isToss ? 'reachUp' : 'reach' })

  // the pan: a short handle in his hand, a rim each side, a bottom
  px.push(...rect(18, top, 19, top, c.panHandle))
  px.push([20, top, c.pan], [27, top, c.pan], ...rect(20, top + 1, 27, top + 1, c.pan))

  // the pancake: flat in the pan, edge-on at the top of its flight
  const flight = [4, 2, 1, 1, 2, 4]
  const y = beat >= 7 && beat <= 12 ? (flight[beat - 7] ?? top) : top
  px.push(...(y <= 2 ? rect(23, y, 24, y, c.pancake) : rect(22, y, 25, y, c.pancake)))

  // steam while it sizzles
  if (beat < 6 || beat > 13) px.push([23, 4 - (t % 3), c.steam], [26, 3 - ((t + 1) % 3), c.steam])
  return px
}

/** Writing: three lines fill the sheet a pixel at a time, then a fresh page. */
function writing(draw: Draw, t: number): Px[] {
  const c = PET.props
  const px = draw(AT_WORK_X, BASE_Y, { eyes: 'right', arms: t % 2 ? 'reachUp' : 'reach' })
  px.push(...rect(18, 2, 25, 8, c.paper))

  const lineLength = 6
  const lines = [3, 5, 7]
  const written = Math.floor(t / 2) % (lineLength * lines.length + 5)
  for (let i = 0; i < Math.min(written, lineLength * lines.length); i++) {
    px.push([19 + (i % lineLength), lines[Math.floor(i / lineLength)] ?? 3, c.ink])
  }
  return px
}

/** Searching: a magnifier held up beside him, a gleam crossing its glass. */
function searching(draw: Draw, t: number): Px[] {
  const c = PET.props
  const beat = t % 14
  const px = draw(AT_WORK_X, BASE_Y, { eyes: 'right', arms: 'hold' })

  // the lens, eight wide and four tall (a terminal pixel is twice as tall as wide, so it
  // reads round): a frame, light glass, a highlight in its upper left
  px.push(...rect(22, 1, 25, 1, c.rim), ...rect(22, 4, 25, 4, c.rim))
  px.push(...rect(20, 2, 20, 3, c.rim), ...rect(27, 2, 27, 3, c.rim))
  px.push(...rect(21, 2, 26, 3, c.glass), [22, 2, c.glint])

  // the handle leaves the lens's lower corner at a true diagonal: two across for one down,
  // a dark collar where it meets the frame, then down to his hand
  px.push(...rect(20, 4, 21, 4, c.collar), ...rect(18, 5, 19, 5, c.lensHandle), ...rect(16, 6, 17, 6, c.lensHandle))

  // the gleam: a slant of light sliding across the glass, then a pause
  if (beat < 5) {
    const g = 22 + beat
    if (g >= 23 && g <= 25) px.push([g, 2, c.glint])
    if (g - 1 >= 23 && g - 1 <= 25) px.push([g - 1, 3, c.glint])
  }
  return px
}

/** Idle: a coffee held close, steam curling slowly up out of it. */
function coffee(draw: Draw, t: number): Px[] {
  const c = PET.props
  const px = draw(CENTER_X, BASE_Y, { arms: 'hold' })

  // the mug, close to him like the pan: a short handle in his hand, coffee showing at the top
  const x = CENTER_X + 17
  const y = BASE_Y + 1
  px.push([x - 1, y + 1, c.mug])
  px.push(...rect(x, y, x + 3, y, c.coffee), ...rect(x, y + 1, x + 3, y + 2, c.mug))

  const rise = Math.floor(t / PET.steamTicks)
  px.push([x + 1, y - 1 - (rise % 3), c.steam], [x + 2, y - 2 - ((rise + 1) % 3), c.steam])
  return px
}

/** Whether his eyes are shut for a blink at tick `t`: every act blinks, now and then. */
function isBlinking(t: number): boolean {
  return t % PET.blinkEvery < 2
}

/** The frame for a mood at tick `t` (one tick per PET.frameMs). */
export function frameFor(mood: Mood, t: number, extras: Extras): Frame {
  const draw: Draw = (ox, oy, pose) =>
    clawd(ox, oy, { ...pose, cap: extras.isNight, isBlinking: isBlinking(t) })
  const glyphs: Glyph[] = []
  let px: Px[]

  switch (mood) {
    case 'idle':
      px = coffee(draw, t)
      break
    case 'think':
      px = cooking(draw, t)
      break
    case 'type':
      px = writing(draw, t)
      break
    case 'search':
      px = searching(draw, t)
      break
    case 'sad': {
      // eyes shut, arms dropped, tears running, two red marks blinking by his head
      px = draw(CENTER_X, BASE_Y, { arms: 'down', eyes: 'closed' })
      for (const eye of [5, 12]) px.push([CENTER_X + eye, BASE_Y + 2 + ((t + eye) % 4), PET.props.tear])
      if (t % 6 < 4) glyphs.push({ cx: 10, cy: 1, char: '!', color: PET.alert })
      if ((t + 3) % 6 < 4) glyphs.push({ cx: 11, cy: 0, char: '!', color: PET.alert })
      break
    }
    case 'party': {
      // a hop, arms up, sparks around
      px = draw(CENTER_X, BASE_Y - (HOP_ARC[t % HOP_ARC.length] ?? 0), { arms: 'up', eyes: 'closed' })
      const sparks = [
        { cx: 0, cy: 1 },
        { cx: 13, cy: 1 },
        { cx: 1, cy: 3 },
        { cx: 12, cy: 3 },
      ]
      sparks.forEach((s, i) => {
        if ((t + i) % 3 !== 0) glyphs.push({ ...s, char: (t + i) % 2 ? '*' : '+', color: PET.spark })
      })
      break
    }
    case 'sleep': {
      // eyes shut, z's drifting up
      px = draw(CENTER_X, BASE_Y, { eyes: 'closed' })
      const drift = Math.floor(t / 8) % 3
      glyphs.push({ cx: 11, cy: 2 - Math.min(drift, 1), char: 'z', color: PET.muted })
      if (drift === 2) glyphs.push({ cx: 12, cy: 0, char: 'Z', color: PET.muted })
      break
    }
    case 'compact': {
      // pressed flat, held, then back up
      const beat = t % 12
      const shape = beat < 3 || beat > 9 ? 'full' : beat < 5 || beat > 7 ? 'squished' : 'flat'
      px = draw(CENTER_X, BASE_Y, { shape, eyes: shape === 'flat' ? 'closed' : 'center' })
      break
    }
  }

  // glyphs are plain ASCII: a Raster cell must be one column wide in every terminal
  return { px, glyphs }
}

// ============ PACKING ============

// quadrant bits: upper-left 1, upper-right 2, lower-left 4, lower-right 8
const QUADRANT = [' ', '▘', '▝', '▀', '▖', '▌', '▞', '▛', '▗', '▚', '▐', '▜', '▄', '▙', '▟', '█']
const DEFAULT_COLOR = 0x01000000
const EMPTY = -1

type Cell = { char: string; fg: number; bg: number }

function paint(frame: Frame): Int32Array {
  const grid = new Int32Array(W * H).fill(EMPTY)
  for (const [x, y, color] of frame.px) if (x >= 0 && x < W && y >= 0 && y < H) grid[y * W + x] = color
  return grid
}

/**
 * One cell from its four pixels. One color: its quadrant over the background.
 * Two colors filling the cell: the larger one's quadrant over the other. Where
 * a cell would need three (two colors and the background), the smaller color
 * gives way: it is a pixel, and the silhouette matters more.
 */
function cellAt(grid: Int32Array, cx: number, cy: number): Cell {
  const quad = [
    grid[cy * 2 * W + cx * 2] ?? EMPTY,
    grid[cy * 2 * W + cx * 2 + 1] ?? EMPTY,
    grid[(cy * 2 + 1) * W + cx * 2] ?? EMPTY,
    grid[(cy * 2 + 1) * W + cx * 2 + 1] ?? EMPTY,
  ]
  const counts = new Map<number, number>()
  for (const c of quad) if (c !== EMPTY) counts.set(c, (counts.get(c) ?? 0) + 1)
  if (counts.size === 0) return { char: ' ', fg: DEFAULT_COLOR, bg: DEFAULT_COLOR }

  const ranked = [...counts.entries()].sort((a, b) => b[1] - a[1])
  const fg = ranked[0]?.[0] ?? EMPTY
  const mask = quad.reduce((m, c, i) => (c === fg ? m | (1 << i) : m), 0)
  const hasEmpty = quad.includes(EMPTY)
  const bg = hasEmpty || ranked.length < 2 ? DEFAULT_COLOR : (ranked[1]?.[0] ?? DEFAULT_COLOR)
  return { char: QUADRANT[mask] ?? ' ', fg, bg }
}

/** The Raster's `cells`: base64 of [codePoint, foreground, background] per cell. */
export function cellsOf(frame: Frame): string {
  const grid = paint(frame)
  const words = new Uint32Array(PET_COLS * PET_ROWS * 3)
  for (let cy = 0; cy < PET_ROWS; cy++) {
    for (let cx = 0; cx < PET_COLS; cx++) {
      const cell = cellAt(grid, cx, cy)
      const i = (cy * PET_COLS + cx) * 3
      words[i] = cell.char.codePointAt(0) ?? 32
      words[i + 1] = cell.fg
      words[i + 2] = cell.bg
    }
  }

  // glyphs only land in cells the pixels leave empty
  for (const g of frame.glyphs) {
    const i = (g.cy * PET_COLS + g.cx) * 3
    if (g.cx < 0 || g.cx >= PET_COLS || g.cy < 0 || g.cy >= PET_ROWS || words[i] !== 32) continue
    words[i] = g.char.codePointAt(0) ?? 32
    words[i + 1] = g.color
  }
  return base64(new Uint8Array(words.buffer))
}

const B64 = 'ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789+/'

function base64(bytes: Uint8Array): string {
  let out = ''
  for (let i = 0; i < bytes.length; i += 3) {
    const a = bytes[i] ?? 0
    const b = bytes[i + 1] ?? 0
    const c = bytes[i + 2] ?? 0
    const n = (a << 16) | (b << 8) | c
    out += B64[(n >> 18) & 63]
    out += B64[(n >> 12) & 63]
    out += i + 1 < bytes.length ? B64[(n >> 6) & 63] : '='
    out += i + 2 < bytes.length ? B64[n & 63] : '='
  }
  return out
}

// ============ VECTOR SURFACES ============

/** One frame as a pixel grid, later pixels on top, for a surface that draws vectors. */
export function pixelsOf(frame: Frame): { width: number; height: number; colors: Int32Array; glyphs: readonly Glyph[]; empty: number } {
  return { width: W, height: H, colors: paint(frame), glyphs: frame.glyphs, empty: EMPTY }
}

