// ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
// ✦ Xiuu · Clawdy · Formatting
// © 2026 Xiuu · Released under the MIT License, see LICENSE.
// ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
import { ALERT_AT, COLORS, WARN_AT } from './config'

// ============ TEXT ============

/**
 * A model id as people say it, for any model to come: `claude-opus-5-5` reads
 * `Opus 5.5`, `claude-haiku-4-5-20251001` `Haiku 4.5`, `opus` `Opus`. Provider
 * prefixes, date stamps, version tags and `[1m]` are dropped.
 */
export function formatModel(id: string): string {
  const base = id
    .replace(/\[.*\]$/, '')
    .replace(/^.*?claude-/, '')
    .replace(/@.*$/, '')
    .replace(/-v\d+(:\d+)?$/, '')
    .replace(/-\d{8}$/, '')
  const words: string[] = []
  for (const part of base.split('-').filter(Boolean)) {
    const prev = words[words.length - 1]
    // a number after a number is the minor version: 5, 5 reads 5.5
    if (/^\d+$/.test(part) && prev !== undefined && /^\d+(\.\d+)*$/.test(prev)) words[words.length - 1] = `${prev}.${part}`
    else words.push(part.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + part.slice(1))
  }
  return words.join(' ') || id
}

export function capitalize(text: string): string {
  return text.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + text.slice(1)
}

export function formatTokens(n: number): string {
  if (n >= 1_000_000) return `${(n / 1_000_000).toFixed(n % 1_000_000 ? 1 : 0)}M`
  if (n >= 1_000) return `${Math.round(n / 1_000)}k`
  return String(n)
}

export function formatReset(iso: string | undefined, now: number): string {
  if (!iso) return ''
  const ms = Date.parse(iso) - now
  if (!(ms > 0)) return ''
  const d = Math.floor(ms / 86_400_000)
  const h = Math.floor((ms % 86_400_000) / 3_600_000)
  const m = Math.floor((ms % 3_600_000) / 60_000)
  if (d > 0) return `${d}d ${h}h`
  if (h > 0) return `${h}h ${String(m).padStart(2, '0')}m`
  return `${m}m`
}

export function shortPath(path: string, home: string | undefined): string {
  let p = path.replace(/\\/g, '/')
  const h = home?.replace(/\\/g, '/')
  if (h && p.toLowerCase().startsWith(h.toLowerCase())) p = '~' + p.slice(h.length)
  const parts = p.split('/').filter(Boolean)
  return parts.length > 3 ? `…/${parts.slice(-2).join('/')}` : p
}

// ============ COLOR ============

export function tone(percent: number): string | undefined {
  if (percent >= ALERT_AT) return COLORS.alert
  if (percent >= WARN_AT) return COLORS.warn
  return undefined
}

function channels(hex: string): [number, number, number] {
  const n = parseInt(hex.slice(1), 16)
  return [(n >> 16) & 255, (n >> 8) & 255, n & 255]
}

/** The color at `t` (0 to 1) between two hex colors. */
export function mix(from: string, to: string, t: number): string {
  const a = channels(from)
  const b = channels(to)
  const out = a.map((v, i) => Math.round(v + ((b[i] ?? v) - v) * t))
  return '#' + out.map(v => v.toString(16).padStart(2, '0')).join('')
}

/** The color at `t` (0 to 1) along a scale of evenly spread stops. */
export function scale(stops: readonly string[], t: number): string {
  const first = stops[0] ?? '#FFFFFF'
  if (stops.length < 2) return first
  const x = Math.max(0, Math.min(1, t)) * (stops.length - 1)
  const i = Math.min(stops.length - 2, Math.floor(x))
  return mix(stops[i] ?? first, stops[i + 1] ?? first, x - i)
}

/** A hex color from hue (degrees), saturation and lightness (percent). */
export function hsl(h: number, s: number, l: number): string {
  const sat = s / 100
  const lig = l / 100
  const k = (n: number) => (n + h / 30) % 12
  const a = sat * Math.min(lig, 1 - lig)
  const f = (n: number) => lig - a * Math.max(-1, Math.min(k(n) - 3, 9 - k(n), 1))
  return '#' + [f(0), f(8), f(4)].map(v => Math.round(v * 255).toString(16).padStart(2, '0')).join('')
}

